---
description: Prefix instance field and method references with this.
globs: **/*.java
alwaysApply: false
---

# Use `this.` for Instance Members

When referencing instance fields or instance methods that can be accessed via `this.`, always prefix them with `this.`.

## Fields

```java
// ❌ BAD
upgradingUnits = new UnitUpgradeContainer();
if (unitsTimer != null) {
    unitsTimer.abort();
}

// ✅ GOOD
this.upgradingUnits = new UnitUpgradeContainer();
if (this.unitsTimer != null) {
    this.unitsTimer.abort();
}
```

## Methods

```java
// ❌ BAD
validateTownPermission(town, permission);
return getClass().getMethod(name);

// ✅ GOOD
this.validateTownPermission(town, permission);
return this.getClass().getMethod(name);
```

## When `this.` Is Not Required

- Static members: use the class name or direct static access, not `this.`
- Local variables and parameters: no `this.` prefix
- `super` calls: use `super.method()`, not `this.super`

When editing existing code, apply this convention to any instance member references you touch.
